{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/mtlsendpointaliases"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/MtlsEndpointAliases","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"MtlsEndpointAliases","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK19MtlsEndpointAliasesV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MtlsEndpointAliases","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MtlsEndpointAliases","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MtlsEndpointAliases","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A TLS listener decides whether to request a client certificate during the handshake,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it has seen any HTTP, so “ask for a certificate on "},{"code":"\/oauth2\/token","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" but not on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\/oauth2\/authorize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"” is not something one listener can do. A deployment wanting both runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, and this object names the second."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only these six are ever aliased. "},{"code":"authorization_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"end_session_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"front-channel and "},{"code":"jwks_uri","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is public key material, so §21.3 rule 2 forbids synthesising"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an alias for any of them — sending a browser to an mTLS host raises a native"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"certificate-chooser dialog most users cannot answer. "},{"code":"issuer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not an endpoint and does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not move either: §12.4 rule 3 still compares "},{"code":"iss","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against it by exact string."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every property is optional"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", though the server’s schema marks all six required. AXIAM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds them from one path through a shared macro and so always publishes the complete set,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but RFC 8705 §5 permits an OP to alias fewer, and the shape of this member must never be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"why a client stops working — the same principle rule 2 point 1 states for the object as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whole, one level in. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" entry falls back to the top-level endpoint of the same name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly as an absent object does.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/MtlsEndpointAliases\/init(from:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\